---
title: "merkle_tree::construct_proofs (Pyth Sui Contracts)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_depth: 1 << depth < len(messages)
    q_check_depth --> q_abort: true, abort E_DEPTH_NOT_LARGE_ENOUGH
    q_check_depth --> q_init_tree: false
    q_init_tree --> q_fill_empty: tree = vector of (1 << (depth+1)) + 1 empty_leaf_hash entries
    q_fill_empty --> q_fill_leaves: fill bottom row with leaf_hash(messages[j])
    q_fill_leaves --> q_fill_nodes: for k = depth down to 1
    q_fill_nodes --> q_compute: node_hash(tree[id*2], tree[id*2+1]) for each level
    q_compute --> q_root: root = tree[1]
    q_root --> q_proofs_init: proofs = empty, i = 0
    q_proofs_init --> q_proof_loop: i < len(messages)
    q_proof_loop --> q_build_proof: true
    q_proof_loop --> [*]: false, return (root, proofs)
    q_build_proof --> q_walk: cur_proof = [depth], idx = (1 << depth) + i
    q_walk --> q_sibling: idx > 1
    q_sibling --> q_walk: append tree[idx XOR 1], idx = idx / 2
    q_sibling --> q_append: idx <= 1
    q_append --> q_proof_loop: append cur_proof to proofs, i = i + 1

    note right of q_fill_nodes
        INV-001: tree uses 1-indexed binary heap layout
        INV-002: parent of node x is x/2, children are x*2 and x*2+1
        INV-003: sibling of node x is x XOR 1
        INV-004: empty leaves use MERKLE_EMPTY_LEAF_PREFIX (2)
    end note
